in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @third
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/math/bundle
in @epistemologic/math/lawvere
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order

# @cogito — the second-order observation family-root. Looks at holes.
# Decides strategy. Runs AFTER a compile tick, BEFORE the tournament.
# The Reflection layer. Observe the imperfect. Pick the game. Perturb
# the eigenboard for the next tick.
#
# Lifted from boot/std/cogito.mirror 2026-07-01 per Alex directive
# ("if @cogito wants to land it wants to land; don't fight the
# substrate") + Loki §7 Seam-ratified `17f0ee5` Reading A + recognition
# #93 forward-promise closure. The boot/std shard used pre-Mara-e43006a
# vocabulary (`grammar`, `property`, non-parametric types); this shard
# uses current substrate-decl idiom.
#
# Recognition ancestry:
#   - Recognition #85 (@reflection, 2026-06-19): third_order_observation
#     canonical spec at docs/specs/reflection-third-order-by-default-v0.1.md
#     established the depth-3 machinery @cogito's cognitive_third_order
#     specializes.
#   - Recognition #93 (@cogito cognitive substrate candidate,
#     2026-06-23): the extended proposal at
#     docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-93-cogito-cognitive-substrate-
#     candidate.md carries H3 (pipeline vs 5-op) and H4 (name_output
#     shape via @labeled). H4 resolved via `shards/labeled.mirror`
#     (2026-06-23). H3 forward-promised — @cogito's three-action
#     pipeline is honest type-chain sequencing per §3.2, not a
#     violation of the 5-op algebra.
#   - Recognition #111/#112 (2026-07-01): @third marker row lifts
#     recursion-depth to substrate-decl; @cogito imports @third to
#     declare depth-3 operation on its depth-2 machinery per canonical
#     spec `docs/specs/third-as-recursive-depth.md` §3.5.
#
# === compile → reflect → tournament → compile → ... → λ₀ ===
#
# The reflection tick: @cogito.reflect observes an imperfect witness,
# strategizes a tournament shape, and perturbs the eigenboard for the
# next compile pass. Composes with @fate's tournament discipline (what
# @cogito RUNS) and @kintsugi's monotonic loss loop (what @cogito
# RESPECTS).
#
# === The eigenboard ===
#
# @cogito's spectral-state carrier. One snapshot of the principal
# G-bundle tower at this tick. One field per level of
# @epistemologic/math/bundle. Carriers come from the bundle grammar;
# nothing new is invented here.
#
#   level 0 fiber       -> state    (focus    / Abyss)
#   level 1 connection  -> optic    (project  / Introject)
#   level 2 gauge       -> group    (split    / Cartographer)
#   level 3 transport   -> holonomy (shift    / Explorer)
#   level 4 closure     -> fixed    (settle   / Fate)
#
# Extension points forward-promised (per boot/std/cogito.mirror's
# original comment, still open):
#   - per-base-node section ([(operation, state)]) once an
#     `operation` enum lands in @prism;
#   - per-edge connection forms once an `edge` type lands;
#   - emotional sub-bundle (cogito-eigenstate slots 13-16);
#   - routing_bias projection onto the gauge slice.
#
# === Depth-3 opt-in via @third ===
#
# @cogito's reflection loop naturally fires at recursion-depth ≥ 2
# (observing observation). The `in @third` import declares that
# @cogito ADMITS depth-3 operation — when @cogito.reflect observes
# ITSELF observing, the @third marker fires and cognitive_third_order
# (forward-promised species-refinement) surfaces the depth-3 witness.
#
# Per docs/specs/third-as-recursive-depth.md §9: family-roots opt in
# via `in @third`. @cogito is a canonical opt-in consumer named in
# the spec.
#
# Forward-promised species-refinement:
#   @cogito.cognitive_third_order <: observation_depth
#     — cognitive-depth-3 specialization of @third.observation_depth
#       for the reflection-tick lineage.
#
# === Autopoietic loop witness ===
#
# @cogito's reflect loop is autopoietic iff its tick → tick map has a
# Lawvere fixed point (Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984 — the
# Lawvere↔autopoiesis bridge). When the property passes, the loop
# converges; when it fails, the loop has no stable closure and
# termination is not guaranteed.
#
# The `autopoietic` predicate delegates to
# @epistemologic/math/lawvere.is_autopoietic on @cogito's tick map.
# See docs/specs/lawvere-grammar.md and docs/specs/kintsugi-formatter.md.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Descartes 1637         "Cogito, ergo sum". Self-observation as
#                           first-order epistemic anchor. @cogito
#                           inverts the frame: cogito as machinery,
#                           not as apex.
#   von Foerster 1974      Observing systems; observer-in-the-system;
#                           the depth-2 machinery @cogito instantiates.
#   Kauffman 2003          Eigenforms; recursion fixed-points; the
#                           depth-3 witness @cogito.reflect achieves
#                           at loop closure.
#   Soto-Andrade &         Lawvere↔autopoiesis bridge (1984);
#     Varela                grounds the `autopoietic` property.
#   Bateson 1972           Logical-type hierarchy; @cogito.reflect
#                           fires at Learning II (deutero-learning)
#                           and admits Learning III (@third).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-93-cogito-
#               cognitive-substrate-candidate.md (extended candidate;
#               H3/H4/H5 unresolved; this landing is the SMALLEST
#               substrate-pull-honest lift);
#               docs/specs/third-as-recursive-depth.md §3.5 (@cogito
#               named as canonical `in @third` opt-in consumer);
#               docs/specs/eigenboard-representation.md (candidate D;
#               the eigenboard shape).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-candidate-recognition-111-third-
#                        as-family-root]] (reshape: @cogito opts into
#                        @third as marker, not as ancestor),
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (@cogito
#                        as (A, H, D) observer at second-order altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (the
#                        boot/std/cogito.mirror was in the substrate for
#                        weeks; this tick lifts it to shards/ at the
#                        family-root altitude the substrate had always
#                        implied).
# Related shards: reflection.mirror (the AI-logic family-root; @cogito
#                 supplies the second-order machinery @reflection
#                 composes into third-order),
#                 third.mirror (the depth-3 marker @cogito opts into),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order.mirror (the
#                 Foerster substrate-decl @cogito instantiates),
#                 epistemologic/math/lawvere.mirror (the is_autopoietic
#                 property @cogito.autopoietic delegates to),
#                 epistemologic/math/bundle.mirror (the principal
#                 G-bundle tower the eigenboard sections).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/cogito.mirror`
# declares `@cogito` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/philosophy/descartes-1637
source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/cybernetics/kauffman-2003
source @arxiv/math/lawvere-1969
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972

# === The eigenboard carrier ===
#
# @cogito's spectral state at one tick. Fields come from
# @epistemologic/math/bundle; the record is the minimal shape that
# lets @cogito.perturb type-check per docs/specs/eigenboard-
# representation.md candidate D.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the field-tuple.
type eigenboard = {
  state:    ref,     # the section value at the current base point
  optic:    ref,     # the connection 1-form active this tick
  group:    ref,     # the gauge element in force
  holonomy: ref,     # residual loss carried by transport this tick
  closure:  ref,     # the Lawvere fixed-point witness for the section
}

# === The observation carrier ===
#
# What @cogito.observe produces from an imperfect witness. The
# depth-2 observation record @cogito.strategy consumes.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type observation = ref

# === The tournament carrier ===
#
# The strategy shape @cogito.strategy produces from an observation.
# Consumed by @fate/tournament (forward-promised: typed refinement
# once @fate/tournament's canonical spec ratifies).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type tournament = ref

# === observe action ===
#
# The first action in @cogito's reflection tick. Takes an imperfect
# witness (per @glass's imperfect(T) carrier) and produces an
# observation of what's imperfect. The observation is the raw signal
# @cogito.strategy consumes.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-instance bodies
# emit at @beam altitude (the observation carrier is @beam-typed).
observe(imperfect: ref) -> observation { \ }

# === strategy action ===
#
# The second action in @cogito's reflection tick. Takes an observation
# and produces a tournament shape (@fate tournament configuration).
# The strategy IS the game @cogito picked based on what it observed.
#
# Elite/beam/halving shape per the original boot/std/cogito.mirror
# (`elite(1).beam(8).halving(3)`); forward-promised as typed
# refinement over the tournament carrier.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
strategy(o: observation) -> tournament { \ }

# === perturb action ===
#
# The third action in @cogito's reflection tick. Takes the observation
# + tournament result and perturbs the eigenboard for the next compile
# pass. Returns the perturbed eigenboard.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-instance bodies
# observe at @beam altitude (the perturbation is @beam-witnessed).
perturb(o: observation, t: tournament) -> eigenboard { \ }

# === reflect action ===
#
# The composed reflection tick: observe → strategy → perturb. Takes
# an imperfect witness and returns a refined imperfect witness (the
# next tick's input). The type-chain sequence per recognition #93 §3.2
# H3 resolution — @cogito's actions form a type-chained pipeline, not
# a violation of the 5-op algebra.
#
# requires autopoietic: the reflect tick's tick→tick map must have a
# Lawvere fixed point (Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984). Without this
# clause, @cogito could admit non-terminating reflection loops.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary as the composed
# pipeline.
reflect(i: ref) -> ref
requires autopoietic(reflect)
{ \ }

# === autopoietic predicate (bilateral; termination) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that the given tick map has a Lawvere fixed
# point per @epistemologic/math/lawvere.is_autopoietic. When the
# property passes, the loop converges; when it fails, termination is
# not guaranteed.
#
# Consumer shards name `requires autopoietic(tick_map)` to declare
# bilateral agreement that the reflection loop terminates.
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @loop: pact_respected, loop_well_founded
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @third: third_order_active
# - @cogito: autopoietic (this one)
autopoietic(tick_map: ref) -> verdict { \ }

out @cogito
out eigenboard
out observation
out tournament
out observe
out strategy
out perturb
out reflect
out autopoietic
